WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.217 --> 00:00:13.779
opened her suitcase and started to unpack.

2
00:00:14.419 --> 00:00:16.700
Her father had already left for a meeting.

3
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.422
"This is going to be so boring," she mumbled.

4
00:00:20.442 --> 00:00:25.805
"How can you have fun when it's dark and cold all the time?"

5
00:00:27.647 --> 00:00:29.948
Isabel and her father lived in Florida.

6
00:00:30.628 --> 00:00:36.013
But for the next month, her father was working at a university in Tromsø, Norway.

7
00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:41.858
The city was north of the Arctic Circle, and they had arrived during the polar night.

8
00:00:42.779 --> 00:00:48.424
Because of Earth's tilt, polar regions receive almost no sunlight during this time.

9
00:00:49.324 --> 00:00:54.689
In Tromsø this lasts from November through January—three whole months!

10
00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.872
Just then Isabel heard a knock.

11
00:01:00.572 --> 00:01:03.513
It was the university student who lived next door.

12
00:01:03.533 --> 00:01:07.035
"Hello," Erik said with a friendly smile.

13
00:01:07.055 --> 00:01:09.456
"Ready for your tour of Tromsø?

14
00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.897
Dress warmly—it's cold outside!"

15
00:01:13.338 --> 00:01:15.979
Isabel forced a polite smile in return.

16
00:01:23.562 --> 00:01:24.062
she thought.

17
00:01:24.082 --> 00:01:27.524
"Right now my friends are probably at the beach!"

18
00:01:30.044 --> 00:01:34.525
Isabel followed Erik as he pointed out restaurants, theaters, and shops.

19
00:01:37.366 --> 00:01:40.047
She spotted a group of kids wearing ski gear.

20
00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:42.988
"Are they going skiing?"

21
00:01:44.528 --> 00:01:45.269
Erik grinned.

22
00:01:45.289 --> 00:01:47.329
"Why does that surprise you?"

23
00:01:47.349 --> 00:01:49.810
"It's dark outside!

24
00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:52.231
Isn't it dangerous to ski now?"

25
00:01:52.251 --> 00:01:54.811
"There are lights on the slopes.

26
00:01:55.151 --> 00:01:56.752
And it's fun to ski at night!"

27
00:01:59.572 --> 00:02:01.894
"What else can you do during the polar night?"

28
00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:03.215
Isabel asked.

29
00:02:04.496 --> 00:02:07.759
"Well, many people go to concerts and cook meals together.

30
00:02:09.121 --> 00:02:11.723
People like to go ice fishing and ice skating.

31
00:02:12.483 --> 00:02:13.845
We can even feed reindeer."

32
00:02:15.546 --> 00:02:16.467
Isabel laughed.

33
00:02:16.487 --> 00:02:21.331
"I could never do some of those things in Florida!

34
00:02:21.872 --> 00:02:26.496
But it must be hard to live with so little sunlight for three whole months."

35
00:02:27.944 --> 00:02:29.505
"Some people find it difficult.

36
00:02:30.686 --> 00:02:34.109
They use special light boxes that give the effect of the sun.

37
00:02:34.849 --> 00:02:36.831
Other people take vitamin D pills.

38
00:02:37.471 --> 00:02:40.553
Not getting enough sunlight can cause a lack of vitamin D."

39
00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:42.855
Erik shrugged.

40
00:02:42.875 --> 00:02:44.936
"I love the polar night."

41
00:02:44.957 --> 00:02:46.978
"What's summer like?"

42
00:02:47.899 --> 00:02:49.420
"Great," Erik said.

43
00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.762
"From May to July, we have the midnight sun.

44
00:02:53.243 --> 00:02:55.104
It stays light all day long.

45
00:02:55.936 --> 00:02:58.939
You can go hiking or swimming in the middle of the night."

46
00:03:03.442 --> 00:03:05.604
They went into a cafe to get warm.

47
00:03:09.707 --> 00:03:11.269
what would you like to do while you're here?"

48
00:03:11.749 --> 00:03:12.450
Erik asked.

49
00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:18.615
"Actually Isabel took a sip of her steaming hot chocolate.

50
00:03:18.635 --> 00:03:20.997
"Everything sounds fun!"

51
00:03:22.518 --> 00:03:24.780
Isabel's month in Tromsø flew by.

52
00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.121
She went skiing and ice fishing.

53
00:03:30.622 --> 00:03:32.603
She sledded down snowy hills!

54
00:03:33.403 --> 00:03:36.225
On her last night in Norway, Erik came by.

55
00:03:41.188 --> 00:03:42.989
have a surprise," he said.

56
00:03:43.009 --> 00:03:47.172
"We're going to drive outside the city for a show."

57
00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:53.896
Forty minutes later Erik pulled into a parking lot.

58
00:03:55.232 --> 00:03:58.914
They got out of the car and followed a trail to a dark field.

59
00:04:01.055 --> 00:04:03.897
People were standing there, staring up at the sky.

60
00:04:03.917 --> 00:04:07.279
"Whoa!" Isabel gasped.

61
00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:11.621
Waves of green light danced above.

62
00:04:11.641 --> 00:04:14.242
"The northern lights!"

63
00:04:15.623 --> 00:04:16.404
Erik grinned.

64
00:04:16.424 --> 00:04:20.566
"They're caused by particles from the sun entering Earth's atmosphere.

65
00:04:21.506 --> 00:04:24.248
You can see the show best when you're close to the North Pole."

66
00:04:31.736 --> 00:04:34.158
Soon they were driving back to Tromsø.

67
00:04:34.178 --> 00:04:39.703
"Ready to return home to warm, sunny Florida?"

68
00:04:40.123 --> 00:04:40.864
Erik asked.

69
00:04:41.845 --> 00:04:43.066
Isabel shook her head.

70
00:04:43.086 --> 00:04:46.448
"Nope! I love the polar night.

71
00:04:46.929 --> 00:04:49.351
It's beautiful—and fun!"
